  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Riake Mahavelon-jafy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In southwest Madagascar, where more than 80% of the population lives on less than $2 a day,&#xa0;overexploitation of natural resources threatens fragile marine and coastal mangrove ecosystems and the&#xa0;livelihoods of ocean-dependent communities in&#xa0;Befandefa,&#xa0;Atongo&#xa0;vaovao&#xa0;and&#xa0;Morombe. By combining&#xa0;traditional knowledge and scientific research, the&#xa0;Riake&#xa0;Mahavelon-Jafy&#xa0;project proposes solutions for&#xa0;sustainable resource management. This initiative combines environmental conservation, economic&#xa0;development, gender&#xa0;equality&#xa0;and social inclusion to&#xa0;set the stage for&#xa0;future projects that will provide sustainable impacts for coastal communities.&#xa0;Specifically,&#xa0;it conducted several studies&#xa0;in parallel, contributing to five different Knowledge Packages (KP), aimed at&#xa0;analysing&#xa0;coastal stakes of the locally managed protected area and informing management structures on specific strategies and intervention opportunities to consider for future projects.</narrative>
  </description>
